---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<Base title={`Privacy — ${site.name}`} description="What Mise stores, what it asks for, and what it never collects.">
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Mise is a macOS menu-bar app. It runs on your Mac. It does not have an account system, and
      it does not include analytics, advertising, or crash reporters.
    </p>

    <h2>What Mise stores</h2>
    <p>
      Sets are stored as JSON on this Mac, in Application Support. Each Set is a name plus a list
      of frames: the app, the display, and the position and size as fractions of that display.
    </p>
    <p>
      Preferences (gap, shortcuts, whether to show a Dock icon) live in the app's standard
      defaults. Nothing in that file is a document, a browsing history, or a keystroke log.
    </p>

    <h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Moving and resizing other apps' windows goes through macOS Accessibility. Mise asks for that
      permission the first time it needs it, not at launch, and opens the exact System Settings
      pane if it is missing. The permission is used to read window frames and to write them back.
      It is not used to observe typing, to scrape other apps' contents, or to run in the
      background as a recorder.
    </p>

    <h2>What Mise does not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No telemetry, usage stats, or unique identifiers sent anywhere.</li>
      <li>No cookies, no website account, no mailing list.</li>
      <li>No network calls in the current release. There is no Mise server.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Mise Pro</h2>
    <p>
      Config sync is a Pro feature. When it ships on a given build, it is opt-in, and this page
      will name the path it uses. Until then, Sets never leave the Mac they were captured on.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The marketing site is static files. It does not set cookies and does not load third-party
      scripts. A download is a file. A page view is a page view.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href="/contact">{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
